Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: a loaded state's pending DMA completions are handled (TODO 415)

A state saved while VIF1's thread was still scanning a display list holds that list's end-of-list interrupt in the
queue of DMA completions, not yet handled. The load put the queue back but left the flag the EE's fast path tests
before it takes the queue as it was at the moment of the load, most often down: the interrupt then waited for the
next DMA to finish while the game waited for the interrupt (vlPS2Internal_WaitForGPU) until its own 3 s lock-up
timeout - a 3-6 s freeze right after loading such a state, every time it was loaded. The flag now follows the queue.
PS2X_STATE_DMAC_FLAG=0: the flag left as it was. A load with completions in the state logs a line either way.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_savestate.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_savestate.cpp
index 2cf6745..a45e779 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_savestate.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_savestate.cpp
@@ -371,6 +371,20 @@ struct PS2StateAccess
         {
             std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(memory.m_completedDmacMutex);
             in.podVector(memory.m_completedDmacCauses);
+            // (TODO 415) The flag the EE's fast path tests before it takes the causes goes with the causes loaded. A state
+            // saved while VIF1's thread was still scanning a display list holds that list's end-of-list interrupt here, not
+            // yet handled; left with the flag of the moment the load came (most often down), the interrupt waited for the
+            // next DMA to finish while the game waited for the interrupt - until its own 3 s lock-up timeout (a 3-6 s
+            // freeze right after a load). PS2X_STATE_DMAC_FLAG=0: the flag left as it was (as before).
+            static const bool keepFlag = []() { const char *e = std::getenv("PS2X_STATE_DMAC_FLAG"); return e && *e == '0'; }();
+            const bool was = memory.m_completedDmacPending.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+            if (!keepFlag)
+                memory.m_completedDmacPending.store(!memory.m_completedDmacCauses.empty(), std::memory_order_release);
+            if (!memory.m_completedDmacCauses.empty())
+                std::fprintf(stderr, "[state] %zu DMA completion(s) / interrupt(s) in the state still to be handled (cause %#x first); "
+                                     "the flag was %s, %s\n",
+                             memory.m_completedDmacCauses.size(), memory.m_completedDmacCauses.front(), was ? "up" : "down",
+                             keepFlag ? "left so (PS2X_STATE_DMAC_FLAG=0)" : "now up");
         }
         in.pod(memory.m_eeTimers);
         memory.m_eeTimerCycles = 0u;
